Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.33 equip panel: ZL / ZR change the partner on the slot list

P6.33 phase 1 (docs/P6.33_ITEMS_MENU.md). On the Status screen's Equipment
panel, while the slot list waits for a choice (STSTATUS_chooseEquipSlot),
ZL / ZR (PAD_L2 / PAD_R2; W / E on the PC keyboard) move to the previous or
next party member, wrapping. The panel keeps the slot cursor and does not
close: StatsScreen.member and EquipPanel.partner change, then the page
(STSTATUS_showChosenPage), the experience, the stats (STSTATUS_previewStats
with slot -1, then STSTATUS_showPartnerStats) and the slots
(STSTATUS_showEquipment) are redrawn with the helpers the question step
uses. The portraits, the party cursor and the slot icons follow
screen->member / panel->partner on their own, every frame.

The switch happens only on the slot list, never inside the item list, so
STSTATUS_previewStats never holds a temporary copy of PartnerStats.equip
across it. Switching writes nothing in GAME: the log line
"dw3-items-menu: partner switch ..." shows the bag and worn totals.

On by default; key items_partner_switch=0 in port_options.cfg (or
DW3_ITEMS_PARTNER_SWITCH=0) turns it off, and then the code path is the
original. Policy in port/items_menu/items_menu.c.

--- a/src/menus/field_menu/equip_panel.c
+++ b/src/menus/field_menu/equip_panel.c
@@ -2,6 +2,9 @@
    panel of STSTATUS_createEquipPanel: its rodata starts at 0x800826CC (USA). */
 
 #include "menus/field_menu.h"
+#if PORT_HOST
+#include "port_items_menu.h"
+#endif
 
 /* Creates the equipment panel's windows: the six slots, the list of items that
    fit the chosen one, their counts, the help and the slot's item */
@@ -262,6 +265,33 @@
     }
 }
 
+#if PORT_HOST
+/* P6.33: ZL / ZR on the slot list change the partner without leaving the
+   panel. Only called between frames of the slot list (never while the item
+   list holds a stat preview). The page, the stats and the slots are refreshed
+   with the helpers the question step uses; the slot cursor stays. */
+static void STSTATUS_portSwitchPartner(EquipPanel *panel, EquipPanelWindows *windows, s32 dir) {
+    StatsScreen *screen = panel->screen;
+    StatsScreenWindows *screenWindows = screen->children;
+    s32 member = dw3_port_items_partner_next(screen->member, screen->count, dir);
+    s32 from = screen->member;
+
+    if (member == from) {
+        return;
+    }
+    screen->previewStats(screen, -1, 0); /* stats as they are, before the switch */
+    screen->member = member;
+    panel->partner = GAME.funcs.getPartyMember(member);
+    STSTATUS_showChosenPage(screen, screenWindows, member, 1);
+    screenWindows->exp->setNumber(screenWindows->exp, 0, GAME.funcs.getPartnerStats(panel->partner)->exp);
+    screenWindows->exp->setRightAlign(screenWindows->exp, 1);
+    STSTATUS_showPartnerStats(screen, screenWindows, 1);
+    STSTATUS_showEquipment(panel, windows, 1);
+    SOUND.playSound(SOUND_CURSOR);
+    dw3_port_items_partner_switched(from, member, panel->partner);
+}
+#endif
+
 /* Choosing a slot: up and down move the cursor, cross lists the owned items
    for the slot ("none" first, then those the partner can equip, then the
    others), triangle closes the panel */
@@ -271,6 +301,13 @@
     s32 n;
     s32 i;
 
